#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198389 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198031 :question/id #uuid "c69a0f41-5b8f-5fcd-b058-94df2d7984bc" :question/math-academy-id "e-12383" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=\\left\\langle z+2y, \\: 3y+z, \\: x -z\\right\\rangle$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=-3x+2y$ for $0 \\leq x \\leq 2$ and $0 \\leq y \\leq 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S} \n=\n\\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{0}^{1} \\boxed{ {\\phantom{A A A A A A A}}} \\: \\text{d}v \\: \\text{d}u.\n$$\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\textrm{d}\\mathbf{S}\n=\n\\iint\\limits_S \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\,\\textrm{d}S\n=\n\\iint\\limits_D \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\cdot (\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v) \\,\\textrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\left\\langle u,\\: v,\\: -3u+2v \\right\\rangle\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (u,v) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq u \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq v \\leq 1 \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-3u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-3⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-3u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-2,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z+2y,\\,3y+z,\\,x-z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=-3u+2v} \\\\  & =⟨(-3u+2v)+2v,\\,3v+(-3u+2v),\\,u-(-3u+2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3u+4v,\\,-3u+5v,\\,4u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨-3u+4v,\\,-3u+5v,\\,4u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨3,\\,-2,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(-3u+4v)\\cdot (3)+(-3u+5v)\\cdot (-2)+(4u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-9u+12v+6u-10v+4u-2v \\\\  & =u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+2y,\\,3y+z,\\,x-z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}u\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}u\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${\\color{blue}u}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a3486150-b3c2-5faf-99d5-b42ced350996" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048185 :topic/difficulty 0.5332953838705958 :topic/id #uuid "8698dcb0-d732-5f62-8605-520598e45185" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198378} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198380}] :topic/math-academy-id 4145 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048253}] :topic/title "Calculating Flux Through Parametric Surfaces"}] :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186731038 :question-generator/id #uuid "3313e0be-0c02-5230-a4e0-04d4c7087033" :question-generator/script "generators/86/860784e2572c4a7860cd46fdd4257b5efc8dfab50238a1211cc264c2e4af3d26/17592186198389.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cea6d00-8d2b-5733-8616-9267687fd149" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423087} {:answer/id #uuid "63293960-e3b1-529e-96e9-642aedf596e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423095} {:answer/id #uuid "84b21f44-ef97-5299-8654-bb5534b15960" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423098} {:answer/id #uuid "cb8fdbef-d72d-513a-8e44-4a96d82e4382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}v-uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423108} {:answer/id #uuid "e83e93b0-2e8f-5324-b1ed-23d683ac8523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63293960-e3b1-529e-96e9-642aedf596e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423095} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ab05865-9935-59ef-90a4-5cba4fa4f3d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194189}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "412e405b-c9a9-5a1c-8e85-45f26189dce3" :question/math-academy-id "q-160887" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨z-y,\\hspace{0.222em}2y-z,\\hspace{0.222em}xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $-2\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u+v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,-2\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u+v} \\\\  & =⟨u+v-v,\\,2v-(u+v),\\,uv⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u,\\,v-u,\\,uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-1)+(v-u)\\cdot (-1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-u-v+u+uv \\\\  & =uv-v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z-y,\\,2y-z,\\,xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(uv-v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{3}uv-v\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198610 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f754a120-8886-56d3-b535-398f13b91c9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398529} {:answer/id #uuid "d28df103-ae23-5647-a506-1bc60c332868" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398530} {:answer/id #uuid "e85142cb-e059-512c-8b7b-18eee7a8c253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398531} {:answer/id #uuid "e433762d-59a0-5efb-bef2-7687d8583f2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398532} {:answer/id #uuid "3a53a3c7-e2f5-50e9-afd4-d3b986017cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(u+v)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e85142cb-e059-512c-8b7b-18eee7a8c253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398531} :answer-field/id #uuid "185487e5-090f-5815-93b2-dfc0c983e691" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398528}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3bcb9d3-050c-5ab9-bd2a-436465223147" :question/math-academy-id "q-161360" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{y}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{z}^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $0\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}u+v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{y}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{z}^{2}⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=u+v} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}(u+v)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨{u}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}(u+v)^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & ={u}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+{v}^{2}\\cdot (-1)+(u+v)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}+{u}^{2}+2uv+{v}^{2} \\\\  & =2uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{y}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2uv)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\color{blue}2uv}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10279bac-75c2-5820-bf33-84359cbf720e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275617} {:answer/id #uuid "397e53f3-63a0-518a-999e-8c3d8631bb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4u+7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275987} {:answer/id #uuid "897e0260-ef83-5fe5-9ee2-95ed9d4cd1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7u+8v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276718} {:answer/id #uuid "bd3f2f9b-ef08-5972-b94d-02717ccd84df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u-7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277162} {:answer/id #uuid "ee6d4a87-66ae-58b1-806a-631ade59590d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7u-8v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10279bac-75c2-5820-bf33-84359cbf720e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275617} :answer-field/id #uuid "8692e3d1-c9bd-5cca-9274-6af9e13d6963" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277965}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bf481ef-95d3-5b3f-b324-29ecd57febda" :question/math-academy-id "q-161358" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\hspace{0.222em}-y,\\hspace{0.222em}2x⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=3x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 5$ and $-3\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}3u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 5,\\,-3\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}3⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,\\hspace{0.222em}2,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\hspace{0.222em}-y,\\hspace{0.222em}2x⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=3u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨3u-2v,\\hspace{0.222em}-v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨3u-2v,\\hspace{0.222em}-v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,\\hspace{0.222em}2,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =(3u-2v)\\cdot (-3)+(-v)\\cdot (2)+2u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-9u+6v-2v+2u \\\\  & =-7u+4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\hspace{0.222em}-y,\\hspace{0.222em}2x⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-7u+4v)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}({\\color{blue}-7u+4v})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b5412c-a9ab-5d1e-8d26-9a4c8f27c8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u+7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275625} {:answer/id #uuid "16ffd34a-40d1-5df6-87ca-5595406b5509" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275691} {:answer/id #uuid "85617ab2-8072-5a8d-9456-259cf0bef230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4v-u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276672} {:answer/id #uuid "ce5a4f92-85cc-5237-ba98-a4e395360811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277305} {:answer/id #uuid "fe69b9d6-2d90-53f7-90a8-f4819b62096e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277710}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10b5412c-a9ab-5d1e-8d26-9a4c8f27c8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u+7v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275625} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a3b6104-863d-512e-9bea-c3b626c9b6e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277943}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "279f5fbf-fc31-5667-8b25-7d1c25dc2d02" :question/math-academy-id "q-161441" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨x,\\hspace{0.222em}y-z,\\hspace{0.222em}x+y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,-1\\le v\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\hspace{0.222em}2,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨x,\\hspace{0.222em}y-z,\\hspace{0.222em}x+y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v-(u-2v),\\hspace{0.222em}u+v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}3v-u,\\hspace{0.222em}u+v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}3v-u,\\hspace{0.222em}u+v⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\hspace{0.222em}2,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-1)+(3v-u)\\cdot 2+(u+v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-u+6v-2u+u+v \\\\  & =-2u+7v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x,\\hspace{0.222em}y-z,\\hspace{0.222em}x+y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-2u+7v)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\color{blue}(-2u+7v)}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "002ddc9f-2c71-5478-8c1d-77a6a8c334bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3u-3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275480} {:answer/id #uuid "023841e2-2821-56a0-955a-89084c15f8d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275496} {:answer/id #uuid "4d835b30-d2dd-53ba-9310-a5a2961e3b3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u+2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276160} {:answer/id #uuid "b4df5cbd-8643-5942-bb9e-8d044eb77815" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u-3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277092} {:answer/id #uuid "f42daa7a-2c08-5500-aa68-d0405d0dc904" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3v+u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277615}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "002ddc9f-2c71-5478-8c1d-77a6a8c334bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3u-3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275480} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca208624-88d6-5a85-8572-2dd062347b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278079}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06f1e075-9f39-52f0-b9b8-c179d2533ffc" :question/math-academy-id "q-161462" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\hspace{0.222em}y+2z,\\hspace{0.222em}2x-y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=y-x$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}v-u⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}-1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\hspace{0.222em}y+2z,\\hspace{0.222em}2x-y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=v-u} \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\hspace{0.222em}v+2(v-u),\\hspace{0.222em}2u-v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v-u,\\hspace{0.222em}3v-2u,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨v-u,\\hspace{0.222em}3v-2u,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-v⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =(v-u)\\cdot 1+(3v-2u)\\cdot (-1)+(2u-v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =v-u-3v+2u+2u-v \\\\  & =3u-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\hspace{0.222em}y+2z,\\hspace{0.222em}2x-y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(3u-3v)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\color{blue}(3u-3v)}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5477038f-1f6e-56c9-abc2-d2382dd8493b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7uv-4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373967} {:answer/id #uuid "938e31d9-0fe9-5c52-a191-c068034a6287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11u-24v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373968} {:answer/id #uuid "73e0a3dc-0594-5177-ad29-6281fad0f7ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373969} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd2d79e-1a1c-53cf-b530-bcceff073bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373970} {:answer/id #uuid "1188f498-8136-53fa-a7c5-2ca872f32cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "938e31d9-0fe9-5c52-a191-c068034a6287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11u-24v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373968} :answer-field/id #uuid "f789f76e-872e-5abd-b18f-ca246f894f3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373966}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "acc5680d-481f-574e-9c37-7723114fd2f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161381" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨z+x,\\hspace{0.222em}y+2z,\\hspace{0.222em}x-4y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-4y$ for $-2\\le x\\le 0$ and $-1\\le y\\le 5.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-4v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 0,\\,-1\\le v\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}2⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-4v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\hspace{0.222em}4,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨z+x,\\hspace{0.222em}y+2z,\\hspace{0.222em}x-4y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=2u-4v} \\\\  & =⟨2u-4v+u,\\hspace{0.222em}v+2(2u-4v),\\hspace{0.222em}u-4v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3u-4v,\\hspace{0.222em}4u-7v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-4v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨3u-4v,\\hspace{0.222em}4u-7v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-4v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\hspace{0.222em}4,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =(3u-4v)\\cdot (-2)+(4u-7v)\\cdot 4+(u-4v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6u+8v+16u-28v+u-4v \\\\  & =11u-24v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z+x,\\hspace{0.222em}y+2z,\\hspace{0.222em}x-4y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(11u-24v)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-1}^{5}{\\color{blue}(11u-24v)}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373986 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f202e15-0fbe-50af-9841-523a939ec510" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373988} {:answer/id #uuid "176843b4-510b-5e14-95d1-94f7f1d2b76b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373989} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb6d1ec-f761-53b6-be0f-80e6cadaee49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u-2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373990} {:answer/id #uuid "73b04bf4-208b-5a5c-aac6-b4ba092785fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373991} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb5f55b-ba54-5712-9575-db91590f82a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u+4v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fb6d1ec-f761-53b6-be0f-80e6cadaee49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u-2v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373990} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a967ea9-62a2-59e7-9156-ea0fff576b7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373987}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "94077de1-f15b-584e-aa54-5f345805312b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161467" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨2x-z,\\hspace{0.222em}y-z,\\hspace{0.222em}z+y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=4x-y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}4u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}4⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨2x-z,\\hspace{0.222em}y-z,\\hspace{0.222em}z+y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=4u-v} \\\\  & =⟨2u-(4u-v),\\hspace{0.222em}v-(4u-v),\\hspace{0.222em}4u-v+v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}-4u+2v,\\hspace{0.222em}4u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨-2u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}-4u+2v,\\hspace{0.222em}4u⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =(-2u+v)\\cdot (-4)+(-4u+2v)\\cdot 1+4u\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =8u-4v+-4u+2v+4u \\\\  & =8u-2v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2x-z,\\hspace{0.222em}y-z,\\hspace{0.222em}z+y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(8u-2v)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\color{blue}(8u-2v)}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398514 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82fdd23c-cc42-585e-88f4-5b182b40e621" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398516} {:answer/id #uuid "23aa505d-ac0a-5049-b866-d1c5cc38bc93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398517} {:answer/id #uuid "e4493f5f-d9a0-53f7-a4c1-2310218fdc19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398518} {:answer/id #uuid "8e689bac-8fa3-596f-82fa-c4985e2215d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398519} {:answer/id #uuid "8b17b653-bdb9-591a-a066-41676556f6e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5u-6v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b17b653-bdb9-591a-a066-41676556f6e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5u-6v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398520} :answer-field/id #uuid "d15555d0-ef8f-523d-8686-3e2c75b76cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398515}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eec4b66c-4af6-5b13-942b-337cb7b8732a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161357" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨x+y,\\hspace{0.222em}2x-y,\\hspace{0.222em}x+z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2x-2y$ for $0\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-2v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}2⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\hspace{0.222em}2,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨x+y,\\hspace{0.222em}2x-y,\\hspace{0.222em}x+z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=2u-2v} \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-v,\\hspace{0.222em}u+(2u-2v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-v,\\hspace{0.222em}3u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-v,\\hspace{0.222em}3u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,\\hspace{0.222em}2,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)\\cdot (-2)+(2u-v)\\cdot (2)+(3u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u-2v+4u-2v+3u-2v \\\\  & =5u-6v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x+y,\\hspace{0.222em}2x-y,\\hspace{0.222em}x+z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u-6v)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}({\\color{blue}5u-6v})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398521 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8c22e69-9068-5d72-8593-ce78861036f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398523} {:answer/id #uuid "2f4db3f6-9c97-526b-8cb2-065c8f5de466" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398524} {:answer/id #uuid "7b2e8a80-65c9-5d70-9b0e-0e801e7e718d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u+v)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398525} {:answer/id #uuid "9f182d4d-0129-52ff-90b2-56e5acb487b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u-v)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398526} {:answer/id #uuid "c1e4fd3a-37bb-5bcd-85c6-185c9a1d61c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+uv-{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8c22e69-9068-5d72-8593-ce78861036f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398523} :answer-field/id #uuid "396da9a4-de3b-5bd7-8b5e-dfc780e10bb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398522}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5e1155b-c484-5f31-a815-946d2d63d6df" :question/math-academy-id "q-161359" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨zy,\\hspace{0.222em}xz,\\hspace{0.222em}xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨zy,\\hspace{0.222em}xz,\\hspace{0.222em}xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=u-v} \\\\  & =⟨(u-v)v,\\hspace{0.222em}(u-v)u,\\hspace{0.222em}uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨(u-v)v,\\hspace{0.222em}(u-v)u,\\hspace{0.222em}uv⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =(u-v)v\\cdot (-1)+(u-v)u\\cdot (1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-uv+{v}^{2}+{u}^{2}-uv+uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨zy,\\hspace{0.222em}xz,\\hspace{0.222em}xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}({u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\color{blue}({u}^{2}-uv+{v}^{2})}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "146aebe7-02b6-58b6-8dd1-374b1fcd30d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423086} {:answer/id #uuid "3586c1bc-3061-5093-99ca-95e798991986" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423088} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1a3ab5-07e2-55d2-b713-d20c37bdda9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423092} {:answer/id #uuid "6197b42b-5e97-5e6b-a1bb-2951dc50be38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423093} {:answer/id #uuid "cacced8e-053e-5057-89f0-678a72c14a18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "146aebe7-02b6-58b6-8dd1-374b1fcd30d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423086} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbc92cc-19ad-54ee-9d42-9ce995a00f4a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29805411-7a4c-51f7-893d-a0f3dc3cef10" :question/math-academy-id "q-161377" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{z}^{2}⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=-x-y$ for $-2\\le x\\le 2$ and $-2\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}-u-v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-2\\le u\\le 2,\\,-2\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}-1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{z}^{2}⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=-u-v} \\\\  & =⟨{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}(-u-v)^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨{u}^{2}-{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}(-u-v)^{2}⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\cdot (1)+({v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2})\\cdot (1)+(-u-v)^{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}-(-u-v)^{2}+(-u-v)^{2} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{y}^{2}-{z}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{z}^{2}⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{u}^{2}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\color{blue}{u}^{2}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b89c0b5-bd8b-5088-a053-0db9bc0fd31f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423085} {:answer/id #uuid "57bc1e11-c92f-5bf5-b1cd-bdfca274f1c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423091} {:answer/id #uuid "62a07ee3-0b12-5f4d-81e0-7183964e0136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3u{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423094} {:answer/id #uuid "876d48e1-3fb3-5bc6-88d3-a7e99ab5d29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv+v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423100} {:answer/id #uuid "b65ee624-a7db-5060-ba14-007644627aeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57bc1e11-c92f-5bf5-b1cd-bdfca274f1c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5uv" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423091} :answer-field/id #uuid "dce1231b-682c-5119-8b60-1e600b81511c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423118}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92e8ddd2-ccb6-5c20-b74b-2f784e857a55" :question/math-academy-id "q-161379" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨(x+y)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}(x-y)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}xy⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=y-x$ for $-1\\le x\\le 1$ and $-3\\le y\\le 0.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}v-u⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 1,\\,-3\\le v\\le 0\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}-1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v-u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨(x+y)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}(x-y)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}xy⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=v-u} \\\\  & =⟨(u+v)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}(u-v)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}uv⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨(u+v)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}(u-v)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}uv⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =(u+v)^{2}\\cdot 1+(u-v)^{2}\\cdot (-1)+uv\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =5uv.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨(x+y)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}(x-y)^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5uv)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\color{blue}5uv}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "556660a7-ba40-5142-a23c-96cdb3bb38b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u-23v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423090} {:answer/id #uuid "86aaa33f-073f-5b9c-b6ed-02e42f1370d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12u-v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423099} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa80cac-9ed0-54f2-a0fb-a71697486081" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8u+14v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423101} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9623af-3bba-5a0d-9c01-61a215703653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5u-17v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423103} {:answer/id #uuid "b721d1da-8cb3-5423-bdff-f515271a77db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-6v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423105}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d9623af-3bba-5a0d-9c01-61a215703653" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5u-17v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423103} :answer-field/id #uuid "de6e4169-2fd0-5a0b-b7fe-172964aca58f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423119}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef91d27f-5ce3-5c48-b5b9-4ec732b3b2e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161471" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨x+z,\\hspace{0.222em}2z,\\hspace{0.222em}y+z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x-3y$ for $-1\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $\\mathbf{F}$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}\\enclose{box}{\\phantom{AAAAAAA}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S}={∬}_{S}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot \\mathbf{n}\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-3v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-3v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\hspace{0.222em}3,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =⟨x+z,\\hspace{0.222em}2z,\\hspace{0.222em}y+z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,y=v,\\hspace{0.167em}\\,z=u-3v} \\\\  & =⟨u+u-3v,\\hspace{0.222em}2(u-3v),\\hspace{0.222em}v+u-3v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u-3v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-6v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $\\mathbf{F}$ and ${\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}) & =⟨2u-3v,\\hspace{0.222em}2u-6v,\\hspace{0.222em}u-2v⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,\\hspace{0.222em}3,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\  & =(2u-3v)\\cdot (-1)+(2u-6v)\\cdot (3)+(u-2v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2u+3v+6u-18v+u-2v \\\\  & =5u-17v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z-y,\\hspace{0.222em}2y-z,\\hspace{0.222em}xy⟩\\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{S} & ={∬}_{D}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))\\cdot ({\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'})\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5u-17v)\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{\\color{blue}(5u-17v)}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}v\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cb970e3-fec2-59c3-a6ab-a3da31447c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - 2 u + 4 v^{2} + 2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533016} {:answer/id #uuid "40978c7c-ce5d-5547-abec-9a813dd99da4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 10 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533030} {:answer/id #uuid "4ff527fd-9ade-5e4f-b140-6b410e0a8d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533039} {:answer/id #uuid "8bae58cd-5720-56b2-94f7-ffdee9f864dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v + 8 uv^{2} + 6 uv - 4 v^{2} - 4 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533054} {:answer/id #uuid "ebdb7518-cf53-5938-8511-2fc4d8f960f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v + 8 uv^{2} + 10 uv + 4 u - 4 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ff527fd-9ade-5e4f-b140-6b410e0a8d2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533039} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fccb2ba-6b05-5811-b0e6-c1883ffe52db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533060}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "242f9872-bf27-5e8a-81c2-046ba61bdf6d" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2 xy + x - y$ for $0\\le x\\le 3$ and $0\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2 uv + u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 3,\\,0\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2 v + 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2 u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 v + 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 v + 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 v + 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 2 v - 1,\\,1 - 2 u,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2 uv + u - v} \\\\  & =⟨2 (2 uv + u - v),\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨4 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩\\cdot ⟨- 2 v - 1,\\,1 - 2 u,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(4 uv + 2 u - 2 v)\\cdot (- 2 v - 1)+(2 uv)\\cdot (1 - 2 u)+(2 u + 2 v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 8 uv^{2} - 8 uv - 2 u + 4 v^{2} + 2 v- 4 u^{2} v + 2 uv+2 u + 2 v \\\\  & =- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv + 4 v^{2} + 4 v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533020 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d7a8d4c-4e17-5501-8857-53f3be2da1d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v + uv^{2} - u + v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533014} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc755dc-f887-5272-97f5-4b9a2c9c3ecb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} - 4 uv + u - v^{2} + v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533025} {:answer/id #uuid "4f5ee7a8-25b7-5f0f-8fb3-0262cf50375a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533038} {:answer/id #uuid "b1f1a002-0ad3-585c-a03c-c4156253e284" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v + uv^{2} + 4 uv + 3 u + v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533064} {:answer/id #uuid "ef98e849-0030-5ffd-8149-2a1ca47cec56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} - u - v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f5ee7a8-25b7-5f0f-8fb3-0262cf50375a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533038} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c81baa9-1eb1-5b7e-ae50-be3131b6b8c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533034}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "321ff97a-842a-5d43-bdf8-efb78e10b9c5" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=- xy - x - y$ for $-3\\le x\\le 4$ and $-2\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-3}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,- uv - u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 4,\\,-2\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,- v - 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & - v - 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & - u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & - v - 1 \\\\ 1 & - u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - v - 1 \\\\ 0 & - u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v + 1,\\,u + 1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=- uv - u - v} \\\\  & =⟨(- uv - u - v),\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- uv - u - v,\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨- uv - u - v,\\,2 uv,\\,2 u + 2 v⟩\\cdot ⟨v + 1,\\,u + 1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(- uv - u - v)\\cdot (v + 1)+(2 uv)\\cdot (u + 1)+(2 u + 2 v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- uv^{2} - 2 uv - u - v^{2} - v+2 u^{2} v + 2 uv+2 u + 2 v \\\\  & =2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,2 xy,\\,2 x + 2 y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}(2 u^{2} v - uv^{2} + u - v^{2} + v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533024 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0932a0b8-0fa3-568b-8122-0d1797e9cf4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3 u^{2} + 2 uv + 3 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533013} {:answer/id #uuid "3e72d819-13b8-5082-b185-e39011021788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533028} {:answer/id #uuid "58b973af-0382-5e69-80b6-ea466d6662d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 u^{2} - 6 uv + v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533042} {:answer/id #uuid "75cd9606-d654-52a8-a5df-a87da24d8731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} - 2 uv - 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533049} {:answer/id #uuid "ee47443a-eea8-51b0-9a9a-89c398f06335" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} + 6 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e72d819-13b8-5082-b185-e39011021788" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533028} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f7dc13a-554c-5bca-a074-a38d478e5b34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533050}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3a7156dc-8a49-52bc-98b0-49852881e07e" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x + 2 y,\\,- x + y,\\,2 - z⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=x^{2} + y^{2}$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u^{2} + v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 u \\\\ 1 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 u \\\\ 0 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 2 u,\\,- 2 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x + 2 y,\\,- x + y,\\,2 - z⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=u^{2} + v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,- u + v,\\,2 - (u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,- u + v,\\,- u^{2} - v^{2} + 2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,- u + v,\\,- u^{2} - v^{2} + 2⟩\\cdot ⟨- 2 u,\\,- 2 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u + 2 v)\\cdot (- 2 u)+(- u + v)\\cdot (- 2 v)+(- u^{2} - v^{2} + 2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 2 u^{2} - 4 uv+2 uv - 2 v^{2}- u^{2} - v^{2} + 2 \\\\  & =- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x + 2 y,\\,- x + y,\\,2 - z⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}(- 3 u^{2} - 2 uv - 3 v^{2} + 2)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533026 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a9ae0c-05c2-5810-b015-e97301bea69e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 10 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533021} {:answer/id #uuid "87acc8e3-7bc7-5f02-9f26-1cb953a6440f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - 2 u - 4 v^{2} - 2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533053} {:answer/id #uuid "8c05f39c-15f2-58ce-a3e4-102d3539e0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533055} {:answer/id #uuid "c76e5c07-3121-53e1-825f-0413889dd45d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v + 8 uv^{2} + 10 uv + 3 u + 4 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533070} {:answer/id #uuid "ffa7c823-f513-584f-ad63-a1f5646d5e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} v + 8 uv^{2} + 6 uv + u + 4 v^{2} + v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c05f39c-15f2-58ce-a3e4-102d3539e0b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533055} :answer-field/id #uuid "a21209f7-71c6-5bfe-99c1-c5b2cccfb0bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533061}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3e4db5c4-da60-5458-9dd4-b7ca956bf947" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,x + y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=- 2 xy - x - y$ for $1\\le x\\le 4$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,- 2 uv - u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- 2 uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,- 2 v - 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- 2 uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- 2 u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & - 2 v - 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & - 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & - 2 v - 1 \\\\ 1 & - 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - 2 v - 1 \\\\ 0 & - 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 v + 1,\\,2 u + 1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,x + y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=- 2 uv - u - v} \\\\  & =⟨2 (- 2 uv - u - v),\\,2 uv,\\,u + v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 4 uv - 2 u - 2 v,\\,2 uv,\\,u + v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨- 4 uv - 2 u - 2 v,\\,2 uv,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨2 v + 1,\\,2 u + 1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(- 4 uv - 2 u - 2 v)\\cdot (2 v + 1)+(2 uv)\\cdot (2 u + 1)+(u + v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 8 uv^{2} - 8 uv - 2 u - 4 v^{2} - 2 v+4 u^{2} v + 2 uv+u + v \\\\  & =4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2 z,\\,2 xy,\\,x + y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(4 u^{2} v - 8 uv^{2} - 6 uv - u - 4 v^{2} - v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533035 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab142e5-68b6-5e46-85e2-53b0af63f72f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 3 uv + 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533015} {:answer/id #uuid "38d189a3-49d7-562c-a5a8-dff53a82b5e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv - u + 2 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533022} {:answer/id #uuid "3e618450-6c32-50ee-9891-cb5a7053df4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 u^{2} v + 4 uv^{2} - 5 uv - 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533027} {:answer/id #uuid "55297ea1-0c27-5ad6-8719-ac0395fb8a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533041} {:answer/id #uuid "9a18d3bd-dd38-5d10-9ccb-e45362470b35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v + 4 uv^{2} - 3 uv + 2 u - 2 v^{2} + 2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55297ea1-0c27-5ad6-8719-ac0395fb8a02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533041} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebd73cc3-9cb5-5ff2-8ee0-589c4c8b7073" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533074}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4cc0069f-c627-527a-995d-c48582128901" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2 xy - x - y$ for $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $0\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2 uv - u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,0\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2 v - 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 uv - u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2 u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 v - 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 v - 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 v - 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1 - 2 v,\\,1 - 2 u,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2 uv - u - v} \\\\  & =⟨(2 uv - u - v),\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 uv - u - v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2 uv - u - v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨1 - 2 v,\\,1 - 2 u,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(2 uv - u - v)\\cdot (1 - 2 v)+(uv)\\cdot (1 - 2 u)+(u + v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 4 uv^{2} + 4 uv - u + 2 v^{2} - v- 2 u^{2} v + uv+u + v \\\\  & =- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(- 2 u^{2} v - 4 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 2 v^{2})\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7436a512-84c9-591c-9ce9-fcc70e1d47ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{2} + 8 uv + 2 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533046} {:answer/id #uuid "8f050df9-ff08-51a6-b322-512385345065" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 6 u^{2} - 8 uv - 3 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533056} {:answer/id #uuid "a8b6cc4a-eef9-568d-bb45-387ac415e38c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 u^{2} - v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533062} {:answer/id #uuid "da71da48-1d04-5e46-96ca-c7e90bbff07c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 u^{2} + 3 v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533073} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b20ec7-b848-5947-b64a-04215b62f1b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533078}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2b20ec7-b848-5947-b64a-04215b62f1b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533078} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf94c05a-12ff-5582-8b0f-1126b1a459c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533072}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ed6e5af-2150-51ed-b676-4ac61ca8579d" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x + y,\\,2 x + y,\\,- z - 1⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=- 2 x^{2} - y^{2}$ for $1\\le x\\le 4$ and $-1\\le y\\le 2.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,- 2 u^{2} - v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,-1\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- 2 u^{2} - v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,- 4 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- 2 u^{2} - v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- 2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & - 4 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & - 2 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & - 4 u \\\\ 1 & - 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - 4 u \\\\ 0 & - 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4 u,\\,2 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x + y,\\,2 x + y,\\,- z - 1⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=- 2 u^{2} - v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨u + v,\\,2 u + v,\\,- (- 2 u^{2} - v^{2}) - 1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u + v,\\,2 u + v,\\,2 u^{2} + v^{2} - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u + v,\\,2 u + v,\\,2 u^{2} + v^{2} - 1⟩\\cdot ⟨4 u,\\,2 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u + v)\\cdot (4 u)+(2 u + v)\\cdot (2 v)+(2 u^{2} + v^{2} - 1)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =4 u^{2} + 4 uv+4 uv + 2 v^{2}+2 u^{2} + v^{2} - 1 \\\\  & =6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x + y,\\,2 x + y,\\,- z - 1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}(6 u^{2} + 8 uv + 3 v^{2} - 1)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03138265-2aad-5cac-aea7-3cb673bb03f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533011} {:answer/id #uuid "2118e949-0da7-5604-af88-a5a5bfc91e01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6 u^{2} - 6 uv + 12 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533018} {:answer/id #uuid "40914390-37f2-59aa-a6d7-afabccbbdd5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 5 u^{2} + 6 uv - 10 v^{2} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533029} {:answer/id #uuid "745222d1-5f79-5053-a65b-b50ff6270bc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 7 u^{2} - 2 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533047} {:answer/id #uuid "f818a851-f2af-5d62-ae5d-ad9d62e92dec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 u^{2} + 2 uv - 14 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03138265-2aad-5cac-aea7-3cb673bb03f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533011} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d6e7828-aa1e-5e60-961d-f41de42d5c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533044}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "74c1515c-d50d-5d9f-a7b8-3c0f3e090bb9" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨3 x - y,\\,- x + 3 y,\\,z + 1⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=- x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ for $-3\\le x\\le 4$ and $-2\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{-3}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,- u^{2} - 2 v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,-3\\le u\\le 4,\\,-2\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,- 2 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- 4 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & - 2 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & - 2 u \\\\ 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & - 2 u \\\\ 0 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3 x - y,\\,- x + 3 y,\\,z + 1⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=- u^{2} - 2 v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- u + 3 v,\\,(- u^{2} - 2 v^{2}) + 1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- u + 3 v,\\,- u^{2} - 2 v^{2} + 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- u + 3 v,\\,- u^{2} - 2 v^{2} + 1⟩\\cdot ⟨2 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3 u - v)\\cdot (2 u)+(- u + 3 v)\\cdot (4 v)+(- u^{2} - 2 v^{2} + 1)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =6 u^{2} - 2 uv- 4 uv + 12 v^{2}- u^{2} - 2 v^{2} + 1 \\\\  & =5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3 x - y,\\,- x + 3 y,\\,z + 1⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{4}(5 u^{2} - 6 uv + 10 v^{2} + 1)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533051 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20356f6f-b037-59be-966f-b091b3698cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 uv + 8 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533017} {:answer/id #uuid "54edc1d0-d27e-5dd3-b36d-d7f4051319b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12 uv + 4 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533040} {:answer/id #uuid "822197f9-d002-5835-967e-4c1e3dcf83c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} - 12 uv - 6 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533052} {:answer/id #uuid "c24b954e-bdab-5c9a-a900-aa62e0e16490" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 u^{2} + 4 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533068} {:answer/id #uuid "cc77d781-d951-5e29-9131-3809cfe9f578" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc77d781-d951-5e29-9131-3809cfe9f578" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533071} :answer-field/id #uuid "acf7f6e2-91ba-5169-9992-db0e3909a286" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533063}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80291a1c-e4f6-54f8-83dc-c6ce18ed1635" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x + 2 y,\\,2 x + 3 y,\\,2 z - 2⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2 x^{2} + y^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 3$ and $0\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2 u^{2} + v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 3,\\,0\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u^{2} + v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 u \\\\ 1 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & 2 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 4 u,\\,- 2 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨x + 2 y,\\,2 x + 3 y,\\,2 z - 2⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2 u^{2} + v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,2 u + 3 v,\\,2 (2 u^{2} + v^{2}) - 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,2 u + 3 v,\\,4 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨u + 2 v,\\,2 u + 3 v,\\,4 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\cdot ⟨- 4 u,\\,- 2 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(u + 2 v)\\cdot (- 4 u)+(2 u + 3 v)\\cdot (- 2 v)+(4 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 4 u^{2} - 8 uv- 4 uv - 6 v^{2}+4 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2 \\\\  & =- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨x + 2 y,\\,2 x + 3 y,\\,2 z - 2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(- 12 uv - 4 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f9a1aa-a390-574f-b1d7-d8bb1b97478b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10 u^{2} - 12 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533012} {:answer/id #uuid "4134b830-3887-598c-b479-3d8b85171c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14 u^{2} + 4 uv - 6 v^{2} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533031} {:answer/id #uuid "995a8e1a-95c0-5a99-b35d-f82c3964898a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 12 u^{2} - 4 uv + 4 v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533057} {:answer/id #uuid "b48be496-3e3d-53b0-838c-eb6f4a85833a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533065} {:answer/id #uuid "c2fb8c43-78cf-570a-b762-20d95c71474e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 14 u^{2} + 12 uv - 2 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b48be496-3e3d-53b0-838c-eb6f4a85833a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533065} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f31fcc4-3134-5b21-936a-7d9e43b33462" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533037}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a222f71-5c1c-5947-8337-693d72d6ebf9" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨3 x - y,\\,- 2 x + y,\\,- z - 2⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=2 x^{2} - 2 y^{2}$ for $0\\le x\\le 4$ and $0\\le y\\le 3.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 4,\\,0\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4 u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,- 4 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 u \\\\ 1 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 u \\\\ 0 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- 4 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨3 x - y,\\,- 2 x + y,\\,- z - 2⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- 2 u + v,\\,- (2 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}) - 2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- 2 u + v,\\,- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨3 u - v,\\,- 2 u + v,\\,- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2⟩\\cdot ⟨- 4 u,\\,4 v,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(3 u - v)\\cdot (- 4 u)+(- 2 u + v)\\cdot (4 v)+(- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 12 u^{2} + 4 uv- 8 uv + 4 v^{2}- 2 u^{2} + 2 v^{2} - 2 \\\\  & =- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨3 x - y,\\,- 2 x + y,\\,- z - 2⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(- 14 u^{2} - 4 uv + 6 v^{2} - 2)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186533067 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "397a6974-dfac-52d9-b5df-0bc50361c68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} v + 2 uv^{2} + 3 uv + u - 2 v^{2} - 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533023} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6a532c-55a0-59d5-b070-81878ff0060b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v + 2 uv^{2} + 5 uv + 3 u - 2 v^{2} - v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533033} {:answer/id #uuid "5b47b261-eaca-5315-bc67-d920b7c6ebbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 5 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533043} {:answer/id #uuid "661f9953-9c2c-5019-8928-9710c30593ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533045} {:answer/id #uuid "b4aae3d5-7110-5af4-87b3-e390ceb9db25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - 2 u + 2 v^{2} + 2 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "661f9953-9c2c-5019-8928-9710c30593ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533045} :answer-field/id #uuid "460785b5-dfe6-5ff3-bd84-f6157544bae8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186533032}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bbbc0ee0-272c-53fb-9af1-c9190cd9e631" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨2 z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩$ and the surface $S$ defined by $z=xy + x - y$ for $1\\le x\\le 2$ and $-1\\le y\\le 4.$ Using the parametrization $x=u$ and $y=v,$ the flux of $F$ through $S$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the flux of a vector field $F$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the parametrization, where $x=u$ and $y=v,$ our surface can be parameterized as\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,uv + u - v⟩\n$$\n\nover the domain \n\n$$\nD=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 2,\\,-1\\le v\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,v + 1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv + u - v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,u - 1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & v + 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & u - 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & v + 1 \\\\ 1 & u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & v + 1 \\\\ 0 & u - 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨- v - 1,\\,1 - u,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $F(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v)) & =⟨2 z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩{|}_{x=u,\\,\\,y=v,\\,\\,z=uv + u - v} \\\\  & =⟨2 (uv + u - v),\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate the dot product of $F$ and ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}) & =⟨2 uv + 2 u - 2 v,\\,uv,\\,u + v⟩\\cdot ⟨- v - 1,\\,1 - u,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =(2 uv + 2 u - 2 v)\\cdot (- v - 1)+(uv)\\cdot (1 - u)+(u + v)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =- 2 uv^{2} - 4 uv - 2 u + 2 v^{2} + 2 v- u^{2} v + uv+u + v \\\\  & =- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}⟨2 z,\\,xy,\\,x + y⟩\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}F(r(u,v))\\cdot ({r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′})\\,\\text{d}A. \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}(- u^{2} v - 2 uv^{2} - 3 uv - u + 2 v^{2} + 3 v)\\,\\text{d}v\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing Flux Over a Surface as a Repeated Integral"}]}
